      "description": "* WHAT...For the Extreme Heat Warning, dangerously hot conditions\nwith high temperatures in the upper 90s to 105 with very warm\nnights with low temperatures in the lower to mid 70s expected. For\nthe Wind Advisory, east winds 15 to 25 mph with gusts to 45 mph\nexpected.\n\n* WHERE...San Bernardino and Riverside County Valleys-The Inland\nEmpire.\n\n* WHEN...For the Extreme Heat Warning, from 10 AM this morning to 8\nPM PDT Thursday. For the Wind Advisory, from 6 AM to 6 PM PDT\nSaturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Gusty winds will blow around unsecured objects. Tree\nlimbs could be blown down and a few power outages may result. Heat\nrelated illnesses increase significantly during extreme heat\nevents.",
      "instruction": "Drink plenty of fluids, stay in an air-conditioned room, stay out of\nthe sun, and check up on relatives and neighbors.\n\nDo not leave young children and pets in unattended vehicles. Car\ninteriors will reach lethal temperatures in a matter of minutes.\n\nWinds this strong can make driving difficult, especially for high\nprofile vehicles. Use extra caution.",
